For a covariant rank-two tensor $T_{mn}$, each lower index receives its own connection correction: $\nabla_sT_{mn}
 =\partial_sT_{mn}
 -\Gamma^t{}_{sm}T_{tn}
 -\Gamma^t{}_{sn}T_{mt}.$ To remember the rule, hold one index fixed as a spectator while differentiating the other, and then repeat for the second index. Contravariant indices receive corresponding terms with the opposite sign.

